    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "https://www.auctioneera.ie/property/23-fairfield-road-farranree-farranree-cork-t23n5d9\r\nImportant note: Details of upcoming viewings and latest offers are available at the Auctioneera website link above.\r\n\r\nAuctioneera is delighted to present 23 Fairfield Road, Farranree.\r\n\r\nWelcome to this charming semi-detached residence located in the well-established and tranquil area of Farranree, Cork. This delightful two-bedroom home offers an inviting curb appeal with its traditional architectural design and front garden, complete with verdant lawns and mature shrubbery that complement the property’s picturesque setting.\r\n\r\nUpon entering, you are greeted by a welcoming hallway leading into a bright and airy living room with large windows that allow an abundance of natural light to flood the space. The heart of the home features a cosy fireplace, perfect for those chilly evenings. Adjacent to the living room, the well-appointed kitchen boasts ample storage and worktop space, providing functionality and convenience for meal preparations.\r\n\r\nThe property’s single bathroom, equipped with modern fixtures, serves both bedrooms, which are spacious and well-lit, offering comfortable sleeping quarters and ample storage potential. The rear garden is notably large and private, not overlooked by neighbouring homes, and presents exciting development potential for future extensions, as many adjacent properties have successfully achieved.\r\n\r\nPositioned a mere 100 metres from essential amenities like a pharmacy and dental practice, this property ensures convenience at your doorstep. Additionally, it enjoys easy access to local transport links, with nearby bus stops providing swift connections to Cork city centre and beyond. The proximity to local schools and sports clubs further enhances the appeal of this location.\r\n\r\nOverall, 23 Fairfield Road is a practical and promising choice for first-time buyers looking to establish a foothold in a quiet yet well-connected community, or investors seeking a property with substantial development potential. Its blend of traditional charm and future growth prospects make it a truly unique offering in today’s market."
